# compiled binaries — never commit build output.
# BUG FIX: the old `*/*.out`, `*/*.o`, `*/*.exe` patterns only match ONE
# folder deep (e.g. helloworld/hello.out), so they silently missed anything
# under a nested folder like controlStructures/if/. `**/` matches at any
# depth, which is what a repo with subfolders inside topic folders needs.
**/*.out
**/*.o
**/*.exe
a.out

# extension-less compiled binaries that have been committed by accident
# in past passes — kept as an explicit safety net alongside the patterns
# above, since a fresh `g++ -o name file.cpp` (no extension) won't match
# *.out/*.o/*.exe at all.
helloworld/hello
input/with
input/without
arithimetic/bscop
arithimetic/cmarthimetic
variables/vartype
variables/valtypedef
variables/valnamespace
variables/varconst
controlStructures/if/baseif
controlStructures/if/baseifelse
controlStructures/if/baseifelseif
